      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.17,
      "end_seconds": 16.5,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "I mean, good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.63,
      "end_seconds": 21.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Right, yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.69,
      "end_seconds": 31.18,
      "duration_seconds": 8.49,
      "text": "Well, I've been having a bit of confusion afterwards. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.83,
      "end_seconds": 35.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Is there any regular medication you use?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.65,
      "end_seconds": 40.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "no, you know, nothing at the moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.92,
      "end_seconds": 46.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.74,
      "end_seconds": 51.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "it's been five days, I'm fairly sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.46,
      "end_seconds": 56.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Is it it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.67,
      "end_seconds": 77.88,
      "duration_seconds": 20.21,
      "text": "mostly mild i've also been biting my tongue, for about four days as for biting my tongue, mostly mild oh, and a fit last month with fit last month, missed sleep and missing tablets definitely sets it off"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.32,
      "end_seconds": 85.32,
      "duration_seconds": 7.0,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. Have you had a bit of confusion afterwards before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.49,
      "end_seconds": 95.32,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened a couple of years ago, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.96,
      "end_seconds": 98.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "What about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.28,
      "end_seconds": 100.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "No. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.78,
      "end_seconds": 107.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Any weakness on one side, loss of bladder control or headache at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.7,
      "end_seconds": 111.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "no, nothing to report there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.32,
      "end_seconds": 115.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.62,
      "end_seconds": 118.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.96,
      "end_seconds": 124.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "What about your tummy and and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.81,
      "end_seconds": 129.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Yeah, bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.26,
      "end_seconds": 142.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.06,
      "end_seconds": 159.34,
      "duration_seconds": 15.28,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. I gave up cigarettes last spring. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day. I walk the dog every morning"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.22,
      "end_seconds": 178.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "What conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.41,
      "end_seconds": 189.56,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "Let me think, I have epilepsy, for about a year. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.44,
      "end_seconds": 196.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "okay, I can see epilepsy in your file as well any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.59,
      "end_seconds": 201.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "no, I've never been operated on"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.81,
      "end_seconds": 206.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.6,
      "end_seconds": 208.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.81,
      "end_seconds": 229.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "You're alert and orientated, speech is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.13,
      "end_seconds": 233.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.16,
      "end_seconds": 244.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Reflexes and power are symmetrical on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.61,
      "end_seconds": 263.11,
      "duration_seconds": 13.5,
      "text": "That's the examination finished. Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like breakthrough seizure on known epilepsy. I can't rule out a provoked seizure from missed medication yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.46,
      "end_seconds": 286.37,
      "duration_seconds": 10.91,
      "text": "I think a blood level of the tablet makes sense here, for adherence check. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.21,
      "end_seconds": 291.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Right, how long will it take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 292.02,
      "end_seconds": 318.92,
      "duration_seconds": 26.9,
      "text": "no driving until we've reviewed you again, I'm sorry, but that's the rule. A short walk every day, even twenty minutes, will help more than you'd think. If you have another seizure lasting more than five minutes, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.01,
      "end_seconds": 325.89,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Okay, you know, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.33,
      "end_seconds": 328.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
